 603          /*
 604           * si5351_set_correction(int32_t corr)
 605           *
 606           * Use this to set the oscillator correction factor to
 607           * EEPROM. This value is a signed 32-bit integer of the
 608           * parts-per-10 million value that the actual oscillation
C51 COMPILER V9.51   SI5351                                                                07/22/2026 12:45:12 PAGE 11  

 609           * frequency deviates from the specified frequency.
 610           *
 611           * The frequency calibration is done as a one-time procedure.
 612           * Any desired test frequency within the normal range of the
 613           * Si5351 should be set, then the actual output frequency
 614           * should be measured as accurately as possible. The
 615           * difference between the measured and specified frequencies
 616           * should be calculated in Hertz, then multiplied by 10 in
 617           * order to get the parts-per-10 million value.
 618           *
 619           * Since the Si5351 itself has an intrinsic 0 PPM error, this
 620           * correction factor is good across the entire tuning range of
 621           * the Si5351. Once this calibration is done accurately, it
 622           * should not have to be done again for the same Si5351 and
 623           * crystal.
 624           */
